a battle royale mode might be coming to  battlefield 2042 assassin's creed could  be getting a god of war styled expansion  and more  tom henderson a long-time journalist  covering the game's industry has  suggested that battlefield 2042's  rumored battle royale mode may be on the  way henderson notes in a recent youtube  video that the battle royale mode for ea  and dice's first person shooter will be  coming in the very near future he does  not mention any specific dates or launch  windows however he does clarify that it  won't surface at least within the next  six months in the meantime some players  have started trying to make their own br  style games in portal and others have  discovered that you can pet the dog or  your ranger in multiplayer henderson  goes on to speak about the next game in  the battlefield series after 2042 saying  he's heard it will be even more like an  overwatch style hero based shooter  specifically he shares that a former  developer with the battlefield franchise  told him the next game has bands of  specialist fighting rather than the  individual specialists in 2042 that  don't have factions  and that's not all henderson has  reported on it was also mentioned that  assassin's creed valhalla's next  expansion could potentially be larger  than both of the game's previous story  dlcs combined the content is expected to  be around 40 hours of additional content  with henderson stating that it will be a  god of war styled expansion whatever  that means earlier this year dataminers  uncovered something related to valhalla  called dawn of ragnarok which might  explain the god of war connection and  suggests that valhalla is planning to  get even more fantastical with its story  after alluding to it earlier this year  ubisoft has announced its first project  within the non-fungible token or nft  ecosystem and it's titled ubisoft courts  an nft is a one-of-a-kind item that  exists on a blockchain that gives buyers  digital ownership rights  courts will wrap up in-game cosmetics  into their own nfts each of which will  have a unique serial number and history  of owners these items called digits can  then be freely traded between players  for agreed upon prices with a natural  economy forming around these  transactions and the scarcity of items  if this sounds familiar it should as  it's essentially what valve has been  doing with the sea marketplace for games  like counter-strike global offensive  dota 2 and more for years the program  which is still in beta is currently only  supported by ghost recon breakpoint on  pc and only available in certain regions  despite using a decentralized blockchain  called tesos the blockchain makes use of  proof of stake as opposed to the  energy-hungry proof-of-work blockchains  such as bitcoin and ethereum leading  ubisoft to call its venture energy  efficient in case you didn't know it can  cost an extreme amount of energy to  produce an nft and comes with a major  cost to the environment which may be why  ubisoft is stressing the energy  efficient angle of tesos this is the  first step in what ubisoft says will be  a four-year venture into blockchain  technology and the company's pursuit of  its own metaverse according to quartz's  press release no other games have been  announced with support for these digits  but given ubisoft's substantially large  library it's perhaps only a matter of  time before that changes ubisoft isn't  the only publisher looking at blockchain  technologies and nfts in particular with  ea and grand theft auto owner take 2  also taking an interest  the first full-length trailer for the  new halo tv series is coming this week  during the game awards but ahead of that  a new teaser video is here to get us  excited filming on the halo tv series  wrapped in july this year following some  delays related to covid but the show is  now in post-production and teams are  knee-deep in finishing the visual  effects and other post-production  efforts ahead of its release on  paramount plus in 2022  what do you think of what we've seen of  the show so far and what are you hoping  to see of it during the game awards let  me know in the comments below and be  sure to leave a like and subscribe so  you don't miss your next gamespot news  you
 

